+Set-operation chains may follow the last `SELECT`.  `INTERSECT [ALL]` binds
+more tightly than `UNION [ALL]` and `EXCEPT [ALL]`, which are equal in
+precedence and associate left to right, so `a EXCEPT b EXCEPT c` means
+`(a EXCEPT b) EXCEPT c` and `a UNION b INTERSECT c` means
+`a UNION (b INTERSECT c)`.  `ORDER BY`, `LIMIT`, and `OFFSET` written after
+the last select apply to the whole chain and are keyed on the combined output
+column names.
+
